# Desktop → web port (permanent)

When porting desktop features to web, the desktop version ([Teslyar75/My_Stamina](https://github.com/Teslyar75/My_Stamina), current release) is **ALWAYS** the reference for functions, content and behavior — **check it before implementing**.

Where a better web-specific solution exists (e.g. tabs/pagination instead of page scrolling, lazy loading), apply it for web, keeping functionality **equal or better**, never cut.

Preserve already successful web solutions (React 19 / TS / Vite / Zustand / FastAPI, PWA, radio host, skins, ContinueHub, Orion zone patterns, cookie-pilot isolation, no-scroll page rule).

Do not copy Tk UI literally. Do not invent features absent from desktop without Sergey's explicit scope. Do not delete user data, force-push, or wipe DBs.

Canonical copies of this rule: root `AGENTS.md`, `docs/web/CURSOR_HANDOFF.md`.
